# `node_modules/` alone is ANCHORED at the build context root, so it does NOT
# match the nested `plugin/node_modules/`. That gap cost twice:
#   1. Earlier session: the host's macOS-arm64 tree was copied into a
#      linux/amd64 image, npm then saw every dep satisfied and installed
#      NOTHING, and the server crashed on boot with "Could not load the sharp
#      module using the linux-x64 runtime". Worked around in the Dockerfile by
#      deleting node_modules before installing.
#   2. Measured 2026-08-13: that workaround fixes CORRECTNESS but not SIZE. The
#      941 MB still lands in the `COPY plugin/ /opt/memsmith/` layer — a Docker
#      layer is a diff, so deleting the files in a later RUN leaves the bytes in
#      place. `docker history` showed that COPY at 996 MB, the single largest
#      layer in the image.
# `**/node_modules/` matches at any depth and excludes it from the context
# entirely, so the bytes are never sent to the daemon.
**/node_modules/
.git/
logs/
.docker-memsmith-data/
.venv
.venv-*
